#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167750} :activity/id #uuid "aa779b94-f579-5a68-8259-42fd1c8580b5" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049506 :topic/id #uuid "fa5d4de4-2fdf-59d1-aea5-7f62da44a307" :topic/math-academy-id 3216} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167750 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168125 :tutorial/content "Consider the circle below. How do we calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x},$ the slope of the tangent to this circle at any point on the circle? \n\n![](images/4c/4cfdf4a02935f6a729b12a81a5b48d0356e37046fb5dabfdeefc498a68b8ed8d.png)\n\nTo calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}$, we start by writing down the equation of the circle. Then, we differentiate the equation of the circle with respect to $x.$\n\nSince our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $\\sqrt{5},$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = (\\sqrt{5})^2 \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx^2 + y^2 = 5.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we differentiate the equation of the circle using implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the slope at any point on the circle using our expression for the derivative. \n\nFor example, since the point $P\\big( \\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3} \\big)$ satisfies the equation $x^2 + y^2 = 5,$ it must lie on the circle. Therefore, the slope of the tangent at this point is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\Bigg|_{( \\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{3})} = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} = -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "69315ade-3415-5abd-94e7-90d616fb7002" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5865 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6af5a081-1dac-5c00-aecb-60e48eb5a180" :step/math-academy-id 35885 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167751}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167751 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166865 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166718 :question/id #uuid "03bebdcd-5908-5c60-b35a-1c8f59593afd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9577"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049470} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049570}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167091} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167092} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262777} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262778} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262779} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262780} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262781}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"} :step/id #uuid "32f917dc-ab34-51bf-8295-5111957c7a29" :step/math-academy-id 35886 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167752}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167752 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166866 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166719 :question/id #uuid "04c9673b-e4e5-508d-acc7-ea0888f2cf87" :question/math-academy-id "e-9578"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049699}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167093} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167094} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262783} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262784} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262785} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262786} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262789} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262790} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262791} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503663}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"} :step/id #uuid "cd16ea49-d32a-5632-8ad6-d600c7a64959" :step/math-academy-id 35887 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167753}} {:db/id #e